3. THE CLI SURFACE, READ READ-ONLY BEFORE ANYTHING WAS CONFIGURED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tool: tools/qmark.py through the wrapper. Exact command:

  CKTO=120 tools/tb qmark tb277 oper1022 u2 115200 --mode 'configure terminal' -- \
      'log facility' 'log facility local5' 'log host' 'log host 10.38.22.33' \
      'log host 10.38.22.33 facility' 'log host 10.38.22.33 facility local1' \
      'no log facility' 'no log host 10.38.22.33'

qmark types `<prefix> ?` with NO carriage return and then clears the line with Ctrl-U, so
nothing is executed (its own self-test proved that first: "self-test OK: 'show clock ?'
then Ctrl-U then CR executed nothing"). This is the only safe way to read AW+ help --
`<cmd> ?` sent through a CR driver EXECUTES the command when `<cr>` is a valid completion
(memory never-send-cli-help-through-a-cr-driver).

