5. STEP 0 -- BASELINE OFF, ON THE WIRE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DESIGNED: with no `log host` and no `log facility` configured, a bounded capture on the
collector leg must contain ZERO syslog packets, while the same capture shows live ICMP,
so the instrument is proved to be watching the right wire. (Measure the feature OFF
first -- memory campaign-measurement-discipline.)

  box:  tools/tb capture tb277 oper1022 eth3 45 s0-eth3.pcap udp port 514 or icmp
  box:  tools/tb ping tb277 eth3 10.38.22.34 4
  DUT:  show clock | include CKT33401-STEP0
        show log config | include Facility      -> Facility: default
        show clock | include CKT33401-STEP0b

  ping:  4 packets transmitted, 4 received, 0% packet loss,
         rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.401/0.842/1.868/0.596 ms

  tools/tb tool tb277 oper1022 syslogwire /tmp/oper1022/s0-eth3.pcap
    syslogwire: /tmp/oper1022/s0-eth3.pcap -- 8 frames in the capture,
                0 syslog message(s) on port(s) 514
      NO SYSLOG MESSAGES. For a control leg that is the measurement, not an error.
    (exit 2)

  The capture filter was `udp port 514 or icmp`, and it holds EXACTLY 8 frames: the four
  ICMP echo requests and the four replies of the 4/4 ping, and nothing else. So the
  instrument was live on the right wire for the whole window and there was no syslog on
  it. The DUT's three marker commands in that window produced log entries locally (they
  appear in `show log`) and NOTHING left the device.

  STEP 0 VERDICT: PASS -- the baseline is silence, measured, not assumed.

