>>> OBSERVATION O-1. `log host <ip>` is a COMPLETE command -- `log host 10.38.22.33 ?`
>>> offers `<cr>` -- and it is accepted with no warning, but on its own it sends NOTHING
>>> EVER. The destination exists in `show log config` with an empty `Filters:` list and a
>>> permanent `0 accepted`. At least one `log host <ip> level <sev>` (or another filter)
>>> is required before a single byte leaves the device. An operator who configures
>>> `log host <ip>` alone gets a device that looks configured, reads as configured, and
>>> is silent.

>>> OBSERVATION O-2, found when adding that filter: the filter cannot be added in one
