6b. THREE MORE EMPTY CAPTURES, AND WHY THEY WERE NOT A DEFECT

  With the filter in place the accepted counter climbed (23 -> 40 -> 45) and the wire was
  still empty in two more bounded windows (30 s at 13:06:29, 40 s at 13:07:42). On the
  device's own evidence the messages were being accepted for that destination and were
  not being sent.

  🔴 A TIMEOUT IS NOT A MEASUREMENT. Rather than write "the DUT does not send syslog",
  the window was widened and the filter opened to all UDP. At 13:08:51 a 40 s capture on
  eth3 returned 12 messages -- and the DUT's OWN messages in that capture explain every
  earlier zero:

    13:09:11.889263 PRI=43 syslog.err    2026 Oct 22 00:08:11 awplus syslog-ng[541]:
                                         Error reading data; fd='17', error='...
    13:09:11.889402 PRI=45 syslog.notice 2026 Oct 22 00:08:11 awplus syslog-ng[541]:
                                         Syslog connection broken; fd='17', s...
    ... the nine messages logged between 00:08:11 and 00:09:11 ...
    13:09:11.889693 PRI=45 syslog.notice 2026 Oct 22 00:09:11 awplus syslog-ng[541]:
                                         Syslog connection established; fd='1...

  All twelve arrived inside 0.5 MILLISECONDS of each other, carrying DUT timestamps
  spanning a full minute. The DUT does not stream syslog here; it BUFFERS and FLUSHES.

>>> OBSERVATION O-3 -- a bench mechanism, not a product defect, and it would have
>>> produced a false FAIL. tb277 has NO UDP/514 listener (and starting one is a root
>>> change on the box, STANDING-ORDERS §4). So every syslog datagram the DUT sends draws
>>> an ICMP port-unreachable from the testbox. The DUT's syslog-ng reads that as
>>> "Error reading data" -> "Syslog connection broken", stops sending, and reopens the
>>> destination exactly 60 s later ("Syslog connection established"), flushing everything
>>> it buffered meanwhile in one burst. Later captures show the cadence exactly:
>>> bursts at 13:11:58.565 and 13:12:58.567 -- 60.002 s apart.
>>>
>>> CONSEQUENCE FOR THE METHOD, and for anyone who runs a syslog case on this bench:
>>> a capture window shorter than ~70 s can land entirely between two flushes and read
>>> ZERO while the feature is working perfectly. Every measurement window in this case
>>> from here on is 170 s, with markers spread across it, so each window is guaranteed to
>>> contain at least two flushes. The three empty windows above are reported here as what
>>> they were -- an instrument artefact of a collector that does not listen -- and NOT as
>>> a property of the DUT.

